  "id": "marlowecrowne-social-desirability-scale",
  "term": "Marlowe–Crowne Social Desirability Scale",
  "definition": "The Marlowe–Crowne Social Desirability Scale is a psychological measure commonly used to assess defensiveness, a trait involving avoidance, denial, or repression of information felt to be threatening. It is used to capture a tendency to present oneself in socially desirable ways, such as conforming to others’ views or minimizing inappropriate behavior or poor performance.",
